      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The analgesic efficiency of Propacetamol and Acid Niflumique for post-operative pain in the recovery room, was studied in two groups of 27 patients who had undergone stripping. Pain scores recorded were obtained with the pain ruler during two hours after intravenous injection of Propacetamol (30 mg/kg-1). The analgesic efficiency of Propacetamol is always good. We have not any benefit to purpose acid nifluril before surgery."},
